{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unrelaxed-gymnastic-pewee","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from bug tapestried-oversize-blackfly: rebar 0.14.0/0.15.0 shipped a capability table that presumed unmeasured models accept `temperature`, and plan review 400'd on Claude Sonnet 5.5 for the reporter. The capability table is only as good as its last measurement. The operator report (suggestion 5) asks for a pre-release probe of the model list.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py:555-565` already probes a Bedrock id bare and with `temperature=0`. The bug's scratch probe (Converse, maxTokens 16, bare / temperature 0 / temperature 1.0 / topP 0.9) classified 17 ids across Anthropic, OpenAI, Moonshot, Amazon, Meta, Mistral and DeepSeek in under 2 minutes.\n\n## Approach (to be designed)\n\nExtend the parity probe to run every model id named in `rebar.toml`, `.github/llm-providers/*.toml` and the capability tables against Bedrock before a release (a `docs/releasing.md` step, runnable locally, portable — not CI-only), and fail when a probed result disagrees with `capabilities_for`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A documented command probes every configured/listed model id and reports disagreements with the capability table (exit non-zero on disagreement).\n- [ ] `docs/releasing.md` lists it as a pre-release step.\n","id":"2bc8-3758-a4b9-47f0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["llm","bedrock","release"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Pre-release probe of configured models' sampling-parameter acceptance"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794424204400025099,"uuid":"4bcdadfa-9cd1-43a8-8a9d-8345660cac5e"}